msgstr ""

#. §0: `x ∉ A × B`
#. §1: `x`
#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `x`
#: Game.Levels.RelationWorld.L01_Cartesianproducts
msgid "As a proof in English, our steps here translate to:\n"
"Since §0, we know that it's not true that the first coordinate of §1 is in §2 and the second coordinate of §3 is in B.\n"
"unfinished"
msgstr ""

#. §0: ```
#. hPQ : ¬ Q → ¬ P
#. ```
#. §1: `hnQ : ¬ Q`
#. §2: `obtain`
#. §3: `exact`
#. §4: ```
#. exact hPQ hnQ
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.L02_arg
msgid "Great! We now have\n"
"§0\n"
"and §1. We can now use the tactics §2 and §3 the same way we did in the last level. Or we can take a shortcut! 👉 Try:\n"
"§4\n"
""
msgstr ""

